      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "5b86ed29afaf320cdb2b927f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I don't see a practical reason why VR controllers are completely disabled in desktop mode. It is possible to own and use Oculus/Vive controllers without an HMD. Using them for locomotion and hand movement doesn't require head tracking or any other functionality exclusive to a headset.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "VR Controls in Desktop Mode",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "59c5267d46c8c20bf1a633f0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "A practical reason is that vrchat doesnt know where your hands should be relative to your head if the HMD isnt on you.\nAlso, both the Vive and Rift controllers send their data wirelessly to the HMDs and then to the PC so they dont work without the HMD.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
